d of  held together these huge empires with  sheer military force and that's within a  very short time most of them just  disintegrated now when you fast-forward  to the United States I actually think  that the United States has had  incredibly strong glue internally for  some reason the American identity has  been very absorptive American culture  people within one generation want to be  Americans and I think that the part of  the secret to that is precisely because  it is an ethnically and religiously  neutral identity so as long as you  embrace American values speak English I  actually think that's very important you  have to be able to participate in the  political sphere to  part you know of the united states but  as long as you believe in the values of  the constitution and are willing to  follow the values than anybody of any  skin color of any background can become  an American and it's been actually I  think a very effective glue there are  dangerous signs that that might be  unraveling if people want to replace  that identity with another formulation I  think that's dangerous but my own view  is that our one of our greatest problems  is really visa vie the rest of the world  I think the United States as a  democratic hyper power right now really  needs to figure out a way to you know  people talk about hearts and minds but  it's even more than that it's it we need  to find ways to convince the rest of the  world that they have a stake in American  success and an American leadership  otherwise you know nobody's going to  want it and that's where we don't have  the glue we can't offer the rest of the  world citizenship from we can't make  them all part of an American Empire I  mean it doesn't seem that we want to do  that so we need to find alternative  mechanisms and I think some of those may  be economic but I think this is the this  is where people should be thinking you  know how can we let other people feel  that they have a stake and that's where  I think the glue you know that's the  hardest question speaking of the rest of  the world you do have a chapter as I  recall I think it's called the  challenger's about some of the other you  don't call them hyper power wannabes I  don't think but but that might be one  way to think of them and I'm not sure  that you think that they actually will  be hyper powers India would be one China  would be one what what does the future  hold for them I do talk about the  European Union and Europe China and  India as you know the rivals that people  worry about a lot these days and  interestingly if my thesis is right that  the way to become a hyper power the only  way you can do it in modern times is by  being able to pull in the best and  brightest from every part of the world  then actually I think that China much as  people are worried I think that China  can continue and will continue to do  extremely well economically it's doing  lots of things  right it will grow and become stronger  but I actually think that it can't  become a hyper power and that's because  China is sort of the opposite of an  immigrant society you know it's an  ethnically defined nation and you for  example still see large numbers of  gifted Chinese engineers and scientists  wanting to come to the United States to  become American citizens but you don't  see large numbers of European and  American engineers moving to China to  try to become Chinese citizens did you  see a lot moving to India you do but I  don't know if they're trying to become  Indian citizens so that's the key it's  you know you could have multinationals  who are located in China but they're  still Americans you know they are not  really they're not trying to be throwing  Chinese citizens so there are I don't  know what the future holds one  possibility is that Europe and China and  India could or Russia could continue to  grow so that they become superpowers you  know or great powers not superpowers I  don't think but superpowers to a certain  point that the u.s. Falls from its hyper  power status and that we go back to a  world where there are just you know  several powers of roughly equal strength  a multipolar world right you know and  that would be quite different from what  we have and I think it's an open  question whether that would be better or  worse for the world or even better or  worse for the United States one of the  points I noticed is that as the meaning  of being a hyper power has changed in  some ways modern hyper powers can't get  all the benefits that past hyper powers  could but they suffer all the costs so  you know we can't just plunder we can't  just plunder we can't just siphon all of  our eyes quietly anyway and even that is  very very difficult I mean you know when  Rome conquered Romania it got a million  pounds of silver and we just can't do  that they didn't have deficit spending  now it is the you know the the the costs  and the advantages of being a hyper  power certainly do do change over over  time well let me ask you one last since  we've just got about a minute left  last question so let's say you even  though we are a democracy that you're  the empress of the of this particular  hyper power and you could you could make  America do two or three things that you  think would be in its own self-interest  what would you have us do well I think  the most important thing is to remember  the formula that has made America so  great and it's I think not been  militarism or invasion or imperialism or  exclusion or arrogance but it's really  simply been tolerance that is this  having the reputation as the most open  and receptive nation in the world and  that's been why we've been able to  attract people from every corner of the  world throughout our history and I think  that's what's giving us our  technological edge and our military edge  so I would say in this moment I feel  that we're in a moment of a lot of  anxiety uh you know maybe after 9/11 our  borders but really not to give in to  sort of this fear and insecurity I mean  even on a personal level with  individuals it's some of the ugliest  moments are when people are afraid that  you give in to kind of scapegoating a  bad tendency so I would say you know we  have a good formula and if we continue  that formula there's really no reason to  think that we can't compete as we always  have  well one like just one last question I  want to make sure that we had time to  get this in so whether we stay a hyper  power or not if yes no answer are we the  last hyper power  I don't know I wish I could give a  better answer but I don't know we may be  because there are not many other great  immigrant societies out there and in the  modern day I don't think there's any  other way to incorporate the world's  best and brightest without being you  know really a magnet and emigrate
 

